die-roll-die

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the software: `die_roll_die/`, `examples/`,
`tools/` and `tests/`.

It does not cover `data/`, which is derived from English Wikipedia and carries
the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence instead.
`data/LICENSE` states that licence, what the material is, and the attribution
that travels with it; `data/sources.json` lists the 100 articles it was built
from with the revision id each was read at.

Redistributing anything from `data/`, modified or not, means keeping CC BY-SA
4.0 and those notices with it. Nothing there restricts what you may do with the
software.
